            "notes": "TOGO M2452 / DSMZ Medium 1076b records the DSMZ Medium 1076b SP4-Z branch using glucose as its energy source. DSMZ Medium 1076b is a 200 ml formula that replaces yeast extract from normal SP4 with fish-sperm DNA, adjusts pH to 7.4, autoclaves at 121 degrees C for 15 minutes, aseptically adds CMRL-1066, autoclaved Yeastolate, heat-inactivated fetal bovine serum, and heat-inactivated swine serum, and then adds either glucose or arginine HCl; the two energy sources should not be combined. This agar-plate branch uses 126 ml distilled water per 200 ml, adds 2 g agar, and is held at 55 degrees C before supplements are added.",
