                "notes": "TOGO M2452 / DSMZ Medium 1076b records the DSMZ Medium 1076b SP4-Z branch using glucose as its energy source. DSMZ Medium 1076b is a 200 ml formula that replaces yeast extract from normal SP4 with fish-sperm DNA, adjusts pH to 7.4, autoclaves at 121 degrees C for 15 minutes, aseptically adds CMRL-1066, autoclaved Yeastolate, heat-inactivated fetal bovine serum, and heat-inactivated swine serum, and then adds either glucose or arginine HCl; the two energy sources should not be combined. This agar-plate branch uses 126 ml distilled water per 200 ml, adds 2 g agar, and is held at 55 degrees C before supplements are added. Corrected TOGO's 200 ml source amounts that had been imported as per-liter concentrations, moved the energy-source solution into the ingredient list as a 10.0 ml/L addition, grounded disclosed simple components and protein hydrolysates, kept opaque product and serum additions intentionally unmapped, and linked the record to DSMZ Medium 1076b SP4-Z."
